m and checked the fix on a\nwatch: Intervals LTHR 172, watch LTHR 168, and a 75–82% target showed as\n129–141 bpm.\n\n## Checked here / not checked\n\n- `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json` now writes `start`/`end` for every\n  HR step, and no `value` keys remain.\n- I did not push anything or check on the watch, because the ground rules\n  rule out calling external services. To confirm: push, read back with\n  `GET /events/{id}`, sync the watch, and check that Tempo shows 151–160 and\n  Float shows 129–141.\n\n## Not done (optional follow-up)\n\nThe same note says steps don't show up in the Intervals web UI unless the\nevent also has a top-level `description` written in Intervals' text grammar.\nThat has nothing to do with the watch bug, and if Intervals can't parse the\ndescription it wipes `workout_doc` too. So I left it out of this fix.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014USNxgD2M4jx5uTtbcJPew","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAsEo9hU73sSo3MZnTEB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the generator. It now names the lower bound of each HR target `start` instead of `value`. I haven't tested it on the API or the watch, because the ground rules ruled out calling outside services.\n\n**The change** is in `gen.py`, in `hr_target()`. Targets now come out as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. They're still percentages of LTHR, so Intervals keeps converting them to bpm from its stored LTHR of 172.\n\n**Why it matters:** the API accepts both key names, but Intervals sends them to the watch differently. With `{value, end}`, the watch snaps the target to its own HR zones, which are based on its auto-detected LTHR of 168. That's exactly what `readback/watch-notes.md` shows: every corridor came out as one of the watch's zone bands. With `{start, end}`, the watch shows the bpm range Intervals worked out. This explanation comes from the note in `notes/exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts.md`, which describes the same symptom and confirms the fix on a watch.\n\n**Checked:** regenerating `plans/tempo-run.json` gives `start`/`end` on every HR step, with no `value` keys left.\n\n**To confirm on the watch:** push the event, sync the watch, and check that Tempo shows 151–160 and Float shows 129–141.\n\n**Left out on purpose:** the same note says steps don't show in the Intervals web UI without a top-level `description`. That's unrelated to this bug, and if Intervals can't parse that description it wipes the steps too, so I didn't add it here. It's listed as an optional follow-up in `ANSWER.md`, along with the full explanation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":24373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1053},"output_tokens":571,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e9fb36-f354-4de8-b6f9-e1dca21fba38","uuid":"5bf5f25a-2852-4797-986c-5df96b1c0da2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:14:07.741Z","request_id":"req_011CgAsEniAGbUo9fKUstEDe"}
